# zzz-302-gs-wrap-blend-grouping: wrapping-blend batches (COLCLAMP=0 shader blend) draw non-overlapping triangles together.
#
# gs_hw_backend.cpp drew every triangle of such a batch with its own glDrawArrays(..., 3) and a glTextureBarrier in between,
# because the shader reads the destination (docs/research/gpu-saturation-2026-11-03.md: N triangles -> N draws and N-1
# barriers). Consecutive triangles whose padded GL pixel rectangles are disjoint now share one draw: ARB_texture_barrier
# defines a feedback draw when each texel is written once and read only by the fragment writing it, and the shader reads
# only texelFetch(uDest, gl_FragCoord). A barrier is issued only before a triangle that touches the current group (at
# most 64 rectangles per group), so the blended result is the same as one draw per triangle. Non-finite extents stay
# alone between barriers. GOW_GS_WRAP_GROUP=0 restores one draw per triangle (A/B and fallback).
# GOW_GS_HW_STATS=1 adds "[gs-hw-wrap] group=<0|1> batches= tris= draws=" every 5 s (draws == tris without grouping).
